# HakiOS fragment: the Qualcomm SDM660 family (Snapdragon 660; "jasmine_sprout", "platina", "wayne") -- what is true of the SoC,
# whatever phone it is in.
#
# The processor has eight cores and the biggest is core 7 (four Cortex-A53 at up to 1.633 GHz, four at up to 2.4576 GHz:
# sdm660_f7a.dtsi:50-242 of the Mi A2's own kernel, qcom,limits-info and the two cpufreq tables at :1406-1424).
#
# The addresses the kernel's drivers carry as defaults are the SC7280's (the reference phone). The ones that differ on this
# chip are NOT changed here: the drivers' defaults are compiled in, and the values that can be given at run time are given in
# the device's soc.args (the IPA, the shared memory, the modem's memory, the RPM's transport, the GPU's SMMU, the IMEM and the
# IPA's streams). The ones with no way to be given at run time are listed in docs/port-notes.md as work to do:
#
#   - the SPMI arbiter's three blocks (the PMIC and the buttons drivers): 0x0800f000 / 0x0800a000 / 0x09400000 on this chip,
#     0x0c440000 / 0x0c40a000 / 0x0e600000 in the drivers
#   - the temperature sensors: one block at 0x10ad000 on this chip, two at 0xc263000 and 0xc265000 in the driver, and the
#     driver's table of 27 sensors is the reference phone's
#   - the virtual timer's interrupt: Qualcomm numbers the EL1 virtual timer PPI 3, which is INTID 19; the driver has 27, the
#     architectural number
#
# What is read of the chip: the identity from the firmware's shared memory (CONFIG_SOCINFO), the clock of the cores
# (CONFIG_CPUFREQ), the temperature sensors (CONFIG_THERMAL) and the PMIC (CONFIG_HAKIOS_PMIC).
#
# Nothing of the phone's is here: the panel, the touch controller, the cameras, the regulators and the buttons are the
# device's own (configs/jasmine_sprout.config).
CONFIG_SOC="sdm660"
CONFIG_CPUS=8
CONFIG_BOOTCPU=7
CONFIG_CPUFREQ=y
CONFIG_SOCINFO=y
CONFIG_THERMAL=y
# the drivers of this SoC family: a device with it gets them from here, whatever phone-specific drivers it leaves out
CONFIG_HAKIOS_CPUFREQ=y
CONFIG_HAKIOS_SOCINFO=y
CONFIG_HAKIOS_THERMAL=y
CONFIG_HAKIOS_PMIC=y
